# 0003. Recommendations from Spark Word2Vec vectors stored in Hive

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-19

Films are recommended by the cosine similarity of Word2Vec vectors trained with Spark on their
text, with films and vectors stored in Hive so the data and training can grow beyond one machine.

## Technical details
- **Storage**: `loaders/` parses the JSON films (`FilmParser`) and inserts them into Hive via
  PyHive (`HiveConnector`, connection from `loaders/config.py`); `loaders/docker-hive/` runs
  Hive locally.
- **Training** (`core/ml_engine/app/main.py`): `SparkWord2Vec` (a `SparkBase` with a Hive
  connection) reads JSON with `FILE_PATTERN`, `prepare()` tokenises `ROW_NAME` into
  `PREPARED_ROW_NAME`, fits `pyspark.ml.feature.Word2Vec(**MODEL_ARGS)` (default vector size
  100), and saves vectors to `TABLE_NAME`.
- **Similarity**: vectors become columns (`vector_to_column`) and similar films are ranked by
  `scipy.spatial.distance.cosine`.
- **Serving**: `core/api/` was planned and never written.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: Apache Spark (PySpark ML), Apache Hive, PyHive, NumPy, SciPy.
- Alternatives: TF-IDF + cosine in scikit-learn (simpler at this size, but doesn't scale out);
  collaborative filtering (needs user ratings the project didn't have).
